WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.550
- You've had mixed reactions

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.330
from people about Princeton, right?

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.163
- Yes.

00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:06.090
- How is that? How do you deal with that?

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.770
- Well, you know, we get a lot of stares.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.360
It's rare where we're from
to see African American

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.019
families with Caucasian babies.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:15.102
- Bye.

00:00:15.102 --> 00:00:16.619
- [Female Guest] (laughs) He's gone again.

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:19.080
And so, we get a lot of stares.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.518
I've had the police called
on me where I've had to

00:00:22.518 --> 00:00:23.351
- [Kelly] What?

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:26.859
- Yes, show documentation
that he's my son.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.250
- Do you get mad at that?

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.090
I would get mad at that.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.320
- You know, we try to just,
kind of push it to the side

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.410
and just choose to love.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.050
- [Kelly] It's almost like you'd rather

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.676
somebody just say something.

00:00:36.676 --> 00:00:37.509
- [Female Guest] Right.

00:00:37.509 --> 00:00:38.667
- Like, instead of like don't stare at me.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.130
I get that it might be weird
but just say something.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.678
- Right. It's just easier to say.

00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:43.204
- [Kelly] I didn't
steal this kid. (laughs)

00:00:43.204 --> 00:00:44.120
- [Female Guest] I know, I know.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.341
- There goes Aiden going after

00:00:45.341 --> 00:00:46.535
- [Female Guest] Right.

00:00:46.535 --> 00:00:47.808
- [Kelly] Y'all are gonna be performers.

00:00:47.808 --> 00:00:49.233
It's your stage y'all! It's your stage.

00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:52.147
- And I'm not the babysitter
because I get that a lot too.

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:54.550
- [Kelly] Oh gosh, oh my gosh.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.383
- Yes, yes. Yep.

00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.216
- [Kelly] People are rude.

00:00:56.216 --> 00:00:58.380
That's like coming up to
ask if someone's pregnant.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.391
Don't do it.

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:00.773
- [Male Guest] No, no. (audience laughs)

00:01:00.773 --> 00:01:01.606
- [Kelly] Don't do it, it's rude.

00:01:01.606 --> 00:01:03.390
- In all fairness, my wife is white

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.860
and so we have biracial kids
and she gets the same thing.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.550
You have a white wife
and my kids, you know,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.010
they look, they're black.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.800
So, sometimes she's at the airport and

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.820
they're questioning the kid,
it was a couple years ago,

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.360
and the kid, she couldn't
talk at the time.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.570
They assume that the
babysitter or something,

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.775
it's just, it's awkward and sometimes...

00:01:19.775 --> 00:01:21.470
- That's so weird, we're
such a multicultural,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.504
- [Male Guest] It's annoying.

00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:23.337
- American's a melting pot of everyone.

00:01:23.337 --> 00:01:24.290
- [Male Guest] Yeah.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.356
- You see it everywhere, I feel like.

00:01:25.356 --> 00:01:26.189
- [Male Guest] It's annoying.

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:28.215
- (audience clapping) I love
that about America. Yeah.

00:01:28.215 --> 00:01:29.170
This is what I love too.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.100
You're open to keeping in contact

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.010
with all the biological parents, right?

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:33.843
- Yes.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:35.650
- I think that that's a really cool thing.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.890
- Yes, it has to be.
You know, I think that

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.826
it's really important
to keep them connected

00:01:39.826 --> 00:01:42.104
to their birth families.

00:01:42.104 --> 00:01:42.937
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:44.740
- I call it my bonus families.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.900
I don't want to ever put
my children in a position

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.810
to where they're questioning
well why didn't you, you know?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.740
Uh-uh, no.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.857
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:52.857 --> 00:01:54.210
- You know, I would rather them know

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.637
and especially that one.

